.SH NAME
EVP_EC_gen, EVP_EC_affine2oct
\&\- EVP routines for EC keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\& #include <openssl/evp.h>
\&
\& EVP_PKEY *EVP_EC_gen(const char *curve);
\& int EVP_EC_affine2oct(const BIGNUM *x, const BIGNUM *y, size_t field_len,
\&                       unsigned char **pbuf, size_t *pbsize);
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBEVP_EC_gen()\fR generates a new EC key pair on the given \fIcurve\fR.
.PP
\&\fBEVP_EC_affine2oct()\fR converts affine coordinates \fIx\fR and \fIy\fR of an EC point
to an octet string conforming to Sec. 2.3.4 of the SECG SEC 1
("Elliptic Curve Cryptography") standard. This octet string can further
be passed to \fBOSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_octet_string()\fR. The length of the field degree
representation (in bytes) must be passed to \fIfield_len\fR. The function allocates
a buffer for octet string and places a pointer to \fI*pbuf\fR. It\*(Aqs the caller\*(Aqs
responsibility to free this buffer with \fBOPENSSL_free()\fR.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUES"
\&\fBEVP_EC_gen()\fR returns the EC key pair generated or NULL on error.
.PP
\&\fBEVP_EC_affine2oct()\fR returns 1 on success or 0 on error.
.SH HISTORY
.IX Header "HISTORY"
\&\fBEVP_EC_gen()\fR was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.PP
\&\fBEVP_EC_affine2oct()\fR was added in OpenSSL 4.1.
